er\",\"text\":\"Micro-learning (2–3 minutes) and problem-scenario formats achieve 75–85% completion. Step-by-step how-to videos also perform well when they're focused and mobile-optimized. The common factor: clarity, brevity, and one clear objective per video.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do training videos need to be professionally produced?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Production quality matters less than relevance and clarity. Authentic employee narration often outperforms polished studio content. That said, poor audio, hard-to-read text, or buffering issues kill engagement. Invest in basics: clear audio, readable captions, and reliable hosting. Professional production adds value when it ensures these standards and matches your company's credibility needs.\"}}]}]}"}></script>
